{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"records\":[{\"exampleId\":\"S141-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"bed87d241f1217c39af859adeb4c4f49a1efc1c745059e70563d49abc5cd5504\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 calls the missing page thoughtful; A5 welcomes financial consequences as added mystery.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 welcomes B2's theft explanation; A5 explicitly uses B4's budget need.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B4 needs budget figures, but A5's appreciation gives B no practical next choice.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 labels B4's consequences interesting without increasing A's involvement.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes missing club minutes; B4 identifies the needed budget figures.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'perfectly shaped question' is concise, though A5 repeats the appreciative tactic.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":80},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"The budget page is missing from our club minutes. Someone's made accounts night interesting.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"The treasurer took it home.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Lovely. A suspect with homework. Shall we ring her?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"She's here. She says she never took it.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"A contradiction in person! Bring her a chair beside mine; I'm staying for the whole meeting.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A treats absent evidence and conflicting accounts as delightful reasons to become more involved.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Generic optimism welcomes good outcomes; this card specifically welcomes uncertainty and suspicion.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A1 enjoys a missing page, and A5 enjoys the mystery's financial consequences.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"This alternative involves collective club business; alternative b makes A's enjoyment disrupt a personal celebration.\",\"reason\":\"Revised within the club setting. Internal reread scores fidelity/logic/relationship/heightening/specificity/wit 5/5/4/4/5/4 = 92: B2 supplies a suspect for A3; B4's denial makes A5 commit to staying and hearing her.\",\"reservation\":\"A's enthusiasm could sound accusatory unless played as sincere curiosity; this remains model review only.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S141-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"94cd982e98168dd4a787a6ef8d9e384f841da92294588e5f7db1f65b8932a6b2\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 celebrates contradictory accounts; A5 regards agreement as spoiling the interest.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 converts B2's possible error into two stories; A5 answers B4's worry directly.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 provide abstract objections without establishing what B needs from A.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 intensifies the preference for uncertainty but makes no consequential next move.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A1 mentions a baker but never identifies the disputed event or its stakes.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'price of tea' is economical, while A5 neatly reverses the expected worry.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":73},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"You ordered our anniversary cake, but the baker says we cancelled. What an intriguing start.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"I have the receipt. It says collected.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Cancelled and collected! Let's ask who collected it.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"He says you did. He has your signature.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"And now I'm involved! Bring the receipt; this is much more personal than dinner.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A experiences contradictory evidence as an invitation to enjoy an increasingly interesting mystery.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Seeking the truth can use identical questions, but this stance makes the unresolved contradiction itself pleasurable.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A3 values having two stories, and A5 explicitly dislikes the prospect of agreement.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Unlike a's club participation, b draws A personally into evidence that threatens an anniversary plan.\",\"reason\":\"Added an anniversary cake setting. Internal reread 5/5/4/4/5/4 = 92: B2's receipt drives A3's collector question; B4 implicates A, prompting A5 to embrace personal involvement.\",\"reservation\":\"The signature is deliberately unexplained; A should welcome investigating it rather than imply a concealed confession.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S142-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"d6d66553461991daf5a077e26f0a1c8d57b630eccb75d8189676b7d566c3905c\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 accepts the secret picnic; A3 tests its explanation and A5 addresses concealing cars.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"B2's school trip causes A3's Sunday objection; B4's cars cause A5's parking question.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B4 changes the transport plan constructively, letting A5 tackle its new concealment problem.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 turns B4's solution into the larger problem of hiding forty adults' cars.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1's secret picnic and rented bus become Sunday's forty adults and cake in A3.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's compact list punctures the school-trip cover; A5 earns its logistical complication.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":92},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"For Dad's surprise picnic, where can forty guests board the bus unseen?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Outside my shop. Dad never goes there.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Good. Tell everyone to arrive separately so the neighbours don't mention a crowd.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Dad's offered to open the shop for me while I organise it.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then board at the library. Ring all forty guests; no group message Dad might see. Who's collecting him after we leave?\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A accepts secrecy and continually translates the plan into practical requirements for maintaining its cover.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Ordinary logistical fussing concerns transport efficiency; this card concerns what observers will notice and believe.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A3 tests whether a school-trip explanation survives scrutiny; A5 asks where the replacement cars can be hidden.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a solves group transport collaboratively; b checks an individual's account against witnesses and timing.\",\"reason\":\"Retained the candidate's family picnic and shop setting, replacing the exposed shopping cover with a library pickup. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, A3 manages witnesses and A5 coordinates concealed communication; logic 5, B2's shop prompts staggered arrivals and B4's shopkeeper Dad forces relocation and separate collection; relationship 4, B2 offers a site and B4 reveals helpful family involvement that compromises it; heightening 4, A5 turns one location change into forty calls and another pickup; specificity 4, A1/B2 establish guests, bus and shop, while library availability remains proposed; wit 4, A5's forty individual calls earn their mundane burden from secrecy. Total 90. Five spoken turns, 73 words; original firstPass preserved.\",\"reservation\":\"The library's suitability still needs B's response, and Dad seeing a group message is a possibility A guards against, not an established fact. The quiet logistical burden needs sincere delivery; this is model review only.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S142-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"d491bef4ffe0c47925cb8bc6bb2003151b306d28c1b6f8304ee8d97313a6572c\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 accepts a cover story; A3 checks the timetable and A5 tests the replacement explanation.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2's 'Exactly' supplies no material beyond A1; B4's walking does specifically cause A5.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B4 adapts the account, but B2 does little to establish the collaborator's pressure.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 adds physical evidence, believable shoes, to B4's six-mile walking explanation.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's last bus at eight and A5's cake make the cover's weaknesses concrete.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's 'believable shoes' compactly makes clothing part of the cover story.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":79},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"For Mum's surprise party, we're saying you brought the cake on the nine o'clock bus?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Yes. She'll ask why she didn't see my car.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"The last bus leaves at eight. Can you claim you walked?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"She drove past me at half eight. I was empty-handed.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then the cake was already here. We need Dad to remember accepting it before his nap.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A supports the secret plan by checking its explanations against schedules, witnesses, and shared recollections.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"An interrogator exposes a false account; A instead helps construct an account that protects an accepted secret.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A5 says 'We need believable shoes,' making A a collaborator in the cover.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a manages visible group transport; b manages family knowledge and a witness's inconvenient observation.\",\"reason\":\"Specified a family surprise party. Internal reread 5/5/4/4/5/4 = 92: B2 identifies Mum as observer, shaping A3's cover check; B4 rules out carrying the cake, so A5 relocates its arrival and recruits Dad's memory.\",\"reservation\":\"Dad's availability remains open; A5 proposes another logistical task rather than guaranteeing a finished cover.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S143-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"53a640fc598b2428c33395db65a026b427bb29a66084c6a68d5278b35936a620\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 isolates red thread and A3 pursues its location, but A5 does not connect it to the entire theft.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"B2's scarf leads to A3's location question; B4's contact makes B the witness in A5.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 answer credibly but reveal no competing need beyond explaining the thread.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 renames B a witness without increasing the thread's explanatory reach.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's missing painting and A3's empty frame provide a clear investigative setting.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's thread acquiring a witness is compact and tied to B4's admission.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":78},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"The painting's gone. That red thread on its frame will explain everything.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"My scarf caught there last night. Can we open the gallery?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"This thread will date the theft. Was the painting there then?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Yes. But I picked that thread off before leaving.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then this one means someone came back wearing your scarf. Keep it on; we'll reconstruct the whole night from this snag.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A makes one ordinary trace the privileged clue through which the whole hidden event must be explained.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"General investigation follows multiple relevant clues; this stance gives one selected detail disproportionate explanatory power.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A1 explicitly sidelines the painting for the thread, and A5 continues centring the thread.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a pressures a fellow custodian about a theft; b recruits a partner into reconstructing A's own morning.\",\"reason\":\"Specified a gallery opening and removed the candidate's solved wedding-gift explanation and competing document. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, A1/A3/A5 make the same thread explain everything, timing and an entire night; logic 4, B2's snag prompts A3's timing question and B4's removal prompts A5's return theory, although scarf identity is an overreach; relationship 4, B2 wants to open while A5 prolongs reconstruction through B's clothing; heightening 4, A5 turns an apparently explained snag into evidence of a return visit; specificity 5, A1/B2 establish missing art, frame, scarf and gallery opening; wit 4, A5's request to keep the scarf on makes the exaggerated inference playable. Total 87. Five spoken turns, 64 words; original firstPass preserved.\",\"reservation\":\"The replacement thread does not prove the same scarf returned. That unwarranted explanatory certainty is A's stance, and B can challenge it; the dialogue neither identifies a thief nor resolves the opening decision. Model reread only.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S143-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"6c7cde6fe2cc0b5ba1dcbab5edd23e9b1ce0455985cb9ad3cd02f81ae7930d4c\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 elevates a coffee ring, but A3 shifts attention to the cup and A5 only names a sequence.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"B2 places the keys in A's pocket; A3's cup 'beside them' lacks a coherent location or time.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 correct A, though neither gives B a clear reason to continue the inquiry.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A5 declares a movement sequence after B4 without showing what new hidden story it exposes.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 gives a coffee ring and keys, but A3 leaves their spatial relationship unclear.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1's ring/key phrasing is compact; A5's abstract 'movement sequence' weakens the payoff.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":59},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"This coffee ring on our holiday map will explain where my keys went.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"They're in your pocket. Can we leave?\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Then the ring explains why we're late. What is it covering?\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"The kennels. You put your mug there when I asked who'd take the dog.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"This ring will explain the whole morning. Put your mug inside it again; we're replaying that conversation until we know how the dog got forgotten.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A insists that one mundane mark can reconstruct the larger story, even after the immediate mystery is solved.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Refusing correction simply denies B's facts; this card absorbs the correction while retaining the chosen clue's authority.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A3 accepts the keys' discovery but continues demanding an explanation through the coffee evidence.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Unlike a's suspicion of another person's access, b uses a helpful correction to investigate A's own behaviour.\",\"reason\":\"Kept the candidate's holiday map and dog-care setting, replacing the multiple-stop audit with reconstruction around the single ring. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, A1/A3/A5 retain the ring as the explanation for progressively larger mysteries; logic 4, B2's correction redirects A3 to delay and B4's remembered question prompts A5's replay, though forgotten dog care remains A's inference; relationship 4, B2 wants departure and B4 recalls B's practical question, while A5 recruits B into another delay; heightening 4, A5 makes the mark govern a reconstruction of the whole morning; specificity 4, A1/B4 establish map, mug and kennels, with lateness compressed; wit 4, A5's resetting the mug earns its procedural excess from B4. Total 86. Five spoken turns, 75 words; original firstPass preserved.\",\"reservation\":\"B4 establishes an earlier dog-care question, not that the dog was forgotten. A's conclusion remains challengeable. Replaying the conversation may help, but A's insistence that this one ring explains the entire morning should carry the disproportionate conviction. Model review only.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S144-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"5ef88cfc7af95dcc25d394eebdb782882220a2ce8d0537d58d98259b115d79b6\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 offers three theories; A3 favours dog and A5 renews theft after different icing evidence.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2's icing supports A3's dog theory; B4's icing on A supports A5's theft switch, though not uniquely.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B4 implicates A personally, preventing A from treating evidence as safely external.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 continues allocating support to theories even when B4 makes A a possible culprit.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's missing cake and B2/B4's visible icing are immediately playable evidence.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's 'renewed funding' extends A1's board language while accepting incriminating evidence.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":86},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Our wedding cake's gone: theft, accident, or the dog. I suspect theft.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"There's icing on him. Get him outside before Mum sees.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Dog leads. I'll take him; check under the table for crumbs.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"That icing's from yesterday. The crumbs lead into the cloakroom.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Theft leads again. Keep the dog here; let's see whether that trail ends at a dropped cake or somebody's coat.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A maintains rival explanations and shifts support as each new clue changes their relative strength.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Serial accusation replaces one suspect with another without testing explanations; A explicitly retains competing theories.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A1 says to keep all three theories, while A3 ranks dog and A5 reopens theft.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a tests cake evidence while B tries to avoid a family discovery; b develops a repair partnership through changing explanations for failed lights.\",\"reason\":\"Kept the wedding setting and removed the candidate's solved hiding scheme and champagne extension. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, A1 supplies three explanations, A3 backs dog and A5 restores theft while explicitly testing accident; logic 4, B2's icing prompts A3's search and B4's older icing plus crumb trail prompts A5's new test, though theft's lead remains provisional; relationship 4, B2 wants discretion before Mum sees and A5 changes B's job to containing the dog during investigation; heightening 4, A5 turns a preferred explanation into a search distinguishing two surviving theories; specificity 5, A1/B4 establish wedding cake and a trail into the cloakroom; wit 4, A3/A5's shifting allegiance repeatedly redirects the same dog-handling task. Total 87. Five spoken turns, 63 words; original firstPass preserved. No pair dialogue or seed provenance changed.\",\"reservation\":\"A cloakroom trail supports movement without proving theft, so A5 must sound provisionally convinced and still willing to test accident. B can resist keeping the dog inside. The S144 bespoke binding remains incompatible for its existing provenance reasons; model review only.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S144-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"3d6f994d31e15662e49d85eaae4a16ffba7f6f0270ea1db24613ec492e236db2\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 supplies three explanations and A3/A5 eliminate them, but only A5 clearly chooses an allegiance.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 uses B2's sunshine; A5 uses B4's unplugging, although unplugging does not establish a shortcut motive.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"B2 and B4 dispense answers without a practical want or changing tactic.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":2,\"evidence\":\"A5 announces the answer already supplied in B4 rather than developing the competing-theory behaviour.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 establishes failed lights but no occasion, location, or urgency.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3's graceful withdrawal and A5's dignity are concise, but mostly decorate elimination.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":66},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"The hall lights failed: weather, wiring, or the caretaker saving electricity. Wiring's my favourite.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"He unplugged them. Help me reach the socket.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Economy takes the lead. I'll hold your ladder.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"The socket's wet. There's rain coming through the roof.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Weather overtakes him. Leave the plug; let's ask whether he unplugged it before the leak.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A lets new clues transfer allegiance among several live explanations and determine the next inquiry.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Simple elimination reaches an answer once; this stance remains willing to reorder previously considered explanations.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A1 names three explanations, with A3 withdrawing weather and A5 selecting the caretaker's shortcut.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a exposes A to suspicion; b makes theory changes guide cooperative handling of a hall problem.\",\"reason\":\"Specified a hall and repair partnership. Internal reread 5/5/4/4/5/4 = 92: B2 displaces wiring in A3; B4 revives weather and changes A5's proposed action and timing question.\",\"reservation\":\"Weather and wiring can coexist causally; A is ranking explanations, not demonstrating that they are mutually exclusive.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S145-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"6a10a1e3bd8027a23e2791cdf17abe49e8a002d4f1bc5c919c50b48c8b4982da\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":5,\"evidence\":\"A1 rejects escape as an interpretation; A5 corrects B4's chasing into escorting.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A3 absorbs B2's distance as an advanced demonstration; A5 specifically corrects B4's proposed chase.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B4 seeks an actionable response, and A5 supplies one while retaining interpretive authority.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5 extends the preferred explanation into how both characters should approach the wardrobe.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"B2 locates the escaping wardrobe halfway down the road, making the impossible problem concrete.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A5's chase/escort correction follows A1's freedom language, though its last sentence explains the joke.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":86},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Our wardrobe isn't escaping. It's exercising its freedom of position.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"It's taking my work clothes down the road. Help me stop it.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"We'll escort it. Ask politely for your uniform; this is a free wardrobe.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"It wants rent for storing my shirts.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"That's a proposal, not a demand. Bring our tenancy agreement; a free wardrobe can negotiate its share of the bedroom.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A maintains final authority over the impossible event by correcting descriptions and actions that threaten A's interpretation.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Impossible Specialist specifies technical handling; this card chiefly protects an authoritative account of what the event means.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"A1 replaces 'escaping' with freedom, and A5 insists on 'escort' to preserve that interpretation.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a frames movement as liberation; b uses ownership of a time doorway to control a household decision.\",\"reason\":\"Kept the liberated wardrobe and supplied B's work clothes as a practical stake. Separate internal reread: fidelity 5, A1/A3/A5 preserve freedom by correcting escape, restraint and demanded rent; logic 5, B2's uniform need causes polite retrieval and B4's rent claim causes a reciprocal tenancy proposal; relationship 4, B2 urgently needs clothing and B4 complicates access; heightening 4, A5 extends furniture freedom into financial responsibility; specificity 5, B2/A5 ground the impossible movement in clothes and a shared bedroom; wit 4, A5's rent negotiation follows B4's claim. Total 92. Five spoken turns, 70 words; no predetermined settlement.\",\"reservation\":\"The wardrobe's ability to communicate enters through B4. A's proposed financial responsibility must sincerely follow the freedom claim, rather than become a detached punishment.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S145-single-b\",\"beforeHash\":\"358516364ea2f352fc74ac8136038924d6c239e062f5a685bb61a95746b85608\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A1 corrects 'broken,' but A3 merely renames the entrance and A5 seeks agreement rather than asserting authority.\"},\"responseLogic\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3 acknowledges B2's wallpaper; A5 introduces uncertainty about sides without using a specific implication of B4.\"},\"relationship\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"B4 wants to shut the doorway, but A5 delays it through an unexplained condition.\"},\"heightening\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A5 adds a temporal puzzle rather than further defending A1's interpretation.\"},\"specificity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1's doorway to yesterday and B2's old wallpaper establish a visible impossible setting.\"},\"brevityWit\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence\":\"A3's 'historically receptive entrance' supplies terminology without a consequential correction.\"}},\"weightedTotal\":62},\"beats\":[{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Our doorway opens to yesterday. It's an extension, not a fault.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"Yesterday's me is coming through to complain.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"Our first visitor. Please make our extension welcoming.\"},{\"speaker\":\"B\",\"text\":\"He says this is his house and we're the visitors.\"},{\"speaker\":\"A\",\"text\":\"He's confusing age with ownership. Show him today's mortgage payment; visiting hours end at six.\"}],\"decision\":\"revised\",\"mechanism\":\"A controls the impossible situation's meaning by overriding rival interpretations with A's own authoritative account.\",\"confusableConcept\":\"Inventing whimsical names alone supplies fantasy vocabulary without the required defence of interpretive authority.\",\"distinguishingEvidence\":\"Original A1's 'not broken' provides the mechanism; the revision extends that correction through A3 and A5.\",\"alternativeComparison\":\"Alternative a corrects a pursuit into an escort; b defends present-day ownership against a rival version of the household.\",\"reason\":\"Kept the time doorway and added a visiting earlier self. Internal reread 5/5/4/4/5/4 = 92: B2 becomes A3's visitor; B4 disputes that status, causing A5 to invoke payment and impose visiting hours.\",\"reservation\":\"The mortgage is comic evidence within A's account, not a resolution of the time paradox or a real ownership rule.\"},{\"exampleId\":\"S146-single-a\",\"beforeHash\":\"c6d874a5f34fbac2c5ef4c86c733f69a5fac9485d33e18fce591cb4b7b3e8590\",\"firstPass\":{\"ratings\":{\"cardFidelity\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence\":\"A1 and A3 revise the deadline confidently, but A5's traffic excuse supplies no clear revised prediction.\"},\